---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Support ClipTown"
  description="Contribute code, testing, design, documentation, or funding to the open-source ClipTown clipboard platform."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Build the town together</span>
      <h1>Support ClipTown with code, testing, design, or funding.</h1>
      <p>The project spans desktop and mobile apps, a Rust API, SDKs, browser integration, encryption, local search, peer sync, and GitOps infrastructure.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</div>
        <h3>Contribute on GitHub</h3>
        <p>Review architecture, open focused issues, improve tests, validate platform constraints, or help implement a repository roadmap.</p>
        <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1.3rem">
          <a class="button secondary compact" href="https://github.com/cliptown" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub organization ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">♥</div>
        <h3>Patreon</h3>
        <p>Support development updates, design work, test devices, code signing, app-store fees, and infrastructure.</p>
        <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1.3rem">
          <a class="button secondary compact" href="https://www.patreon.com/cliptown" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ClipTown on Patreon ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">★</div>
        <h3>GitHub Sponsors</h3>
        <p>Use GitHub's sponsorship surface when it is available for the organization owner and linked ClipTown work.</p>
        <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1.3rem">
          <a class="button secondary compact" href="https://github.com/sponsors/ORESoftware" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub Sponsors ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="callout">
        The Patreon URL was not discoverable in public search when this page was built. Treat it as the intended creator URL and verify or replace it before announcing a funding launch.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">High-value help</span></div>
        <div>
          <h2>Contributions that unlock releases.</h2>
          <p>The most useful work reduces platform, privacy, and release risk rather than merely adding surface area.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-grid">
        <article class="detail-card">
          <h3>Platform testing</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>macOS menu-bar, permissions, signing, and notarization.</li>
            <li>Windows tray, ARM64, installer, and credential storage.</li>
            <li>iOS/Android share, keyboard, privacy, and store review behavior.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="detail-card">
          <h3>Security review</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Key hierarchy, device enrollment, recovery, and revocation.</li>
            <li>Blind-index and embedding privacy analysis.</li>
            <li>Peer pairing, replay protection, and deterministic sync.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="detail-card">
          <h3>Product design</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Keyboard-first search and accessibility.</li>
            <li>Image, file, and rich-content previews.</li>
            <li>Clear consent and exclusion controls for passive capture.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="detail-card">
          <h3>Release engineering</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Signed multi-platform artifacts and provenance.</li>
            <li>App-store metadata, privacy manifests, and screenshots.</li>
            <li>GitHub Pages, changelog, release notes, and update channels.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
